87: 
88: At kagi revision `c49023b773b69de983f0e6eb7e5867ceb5c2c634`, `corpus/drift-pins.sh` lines 400 and 403 use `grep -q "$3" <<< "$out"` to search expected verdict words as unanchored regular expressions. Line 158 prints `DRIFT   %s %s` with path text, which can contaminate such a word search; it is a diagnostic producer, not itself a grep.
89: 
90: Recommendation to kagi: anchor the intended verdict record and distinguish it from path-bearing diagnostics; preserve separate pass/fail assertions. No kagi file was edited. This handoff is included in the round-58 fleet report.
